General Decision: Don't use

1. PCAN's repo was last updated in 2019, without leaving any specification of packages - hence environment could be faulty and produce silent errors
2. PCAN operates on tensorflow < 2.0, which is (opinion) not usable by todays standards. Authors deliver Pytorch version, but it's already different model and idea (2022)
3. Repository has dependencies from matlab
4. Pretrained weights delivered by authors are faulty (still probably because of environment mismatch). 